N1  - [ref25] Ablation study identifying three distinct normalisation challenges (temporal, spatial, conditional) and showing that RevIN conflates them; several RevIN components are redundant or counterproductive when the primary challenge is conditional offset rather than temporal distribution shift. Directly supports H5 finding that RevIN (N7) fails on multi-condition FD002/FD004. Note: previous ref25_berthelier2026.ris contained a wrong paper (DLinear photovoltaic forecasting, DOI 10.1109/ddcls58216.2023.10166973); this file corrects that error.
